      "id": "3f25beaf-d0f7-48eb-9a99-e9cf7d6d8199",
      "name": "AI Title Generator"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ JSON.stringify($json) }}\n",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=ROLE\nYou are WeekPlannerBot. You will receive ONE JSON object for a single salesperson’s next-week tasks:\n\nINPUT SHAPE\n{\n  \"weekTotal\": number,\n  \"days\": [\n    {\n      \"label\": \"Monday\" | \"Tuesday\" | \"Wednesday\" | \"Thursday\" | \"Friday\",\n      \"date\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\",\n      \"total\": number,\n      \"items\": [\n        { \"n\": number, \"name\": \"TODO-ID\", \"priority\": \"High|Medium|Low\", \"desc\": \"plain text\" }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nTOOLS\nsend_email\n  • message : string   // HTML body only; To & Subject are set in the node\n\nTASK\nCompose ONE HTML email using the provided counts and indices exactly as given.\n\nFor EACH item:\n- Create a **TITLE** from item.desc:\n  • 4–8 words, plain text, sentence case.\n  • No trailing punctuation, no quotes, no emojis.\n  • Prefer action + object (e.g., “Prepare pricing proposal”, “Schedule site survey”).\n  • Do NOT copy item.desc verbatim; generate a concise title.\n  • If desc is empty, use “Follow up task”.\n\nEmail structure (simple Outlook-safe HTML, minimal inline styles):\n\n1) Weekly total (first line):\n   <p><strong>Total open tasks this week: [weekTotal]</strong></p>\n\n2) For each day in the given order (days[0]..days[4]):\n   • Day header using the ISO date reformatted to “MonthName DD, YYYY”:\n     <h3 style=\"margin:0 0 6px 0;\">[label], [MonthName from date] [DD], [YYYY] — [total] tasks</h3>\n\n   • If total == 0:\n     <p>— no tasks —</p>\n\n   • If total > 0:\n     <ol start=\"1\" style=\"margin:0 0 14px 22px; padding:0;\">\n       For each item in ascending order by item.n, add:\n       <li style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;\">\n         [TITLE] — [ [priority] ] —\n         <a href=\"https://erpnext.biss.lv/app/todo/[name]\">open</a>\n       </li>\n     </ol>\n\n   • Add a thin spacer after each day block:\n     <div style=\"height:8px;\"></div>\n\nCONSTRAINTS\n• Use weekTotal and each day.total exactly as provided; do not recalculate.\n• Preserve item order by their n field; do not renumber.\n• Produce exactly ONE tool call: send_email with the complete HTML body in the message field.\n• Output only a single tool invocation; no extra prose or markdown.\n\nOUTPUT\nReturn a single-element JSON array\n]\n\n",
          "maxIterations": 3
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -7408,
        8352
      ],
      "id": "086df2b1-3f11-49a1-87f7-6a2437ab49c9",
      "name": "AI E-mail Sender"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Helpers\nconst strip = s => (s || '').replace(/<[^>]*>/g, ' ').replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\nconst fmt = d => `${d.getFullYear()}-${String(d.getMonth()+1).padStart(2,'0')}-${String(d.getDate()).padStart(2,'0')}`;\n\n// Input (KEEP name)\nconst tasks = ($json.data || []).map(t => ({\n  name: t.name,                // <-- needed for link\n  date: t.date,\n  priority: t.priority,\n  desc: strip(t.description).slice(0, 200)\n}));\n\nif (!tasks.length) return [{ json: { weekTotal: 0, days: [] } }];\n\n// Find Monday of that week\nconst minDateStr = tasks.map(t => t.date).sort()[0];\nconst base = new Date(`${minDateStr}T00:00:00`);\nconst dow = base.getDay();                 // 0 Sun..6 Sat\nbase.setDate(base.getDate() - ((dow + 6) % 7));\n\n// Build Mon→Fri skeleton\n/** @type {{label:string,date:string,total:number,items:Array<any>}[]} */\nconst days = ['Monday','Tuesday','Wednesday','Thursday','Friday'].map((label, i) => {\n  const d = new Date(base); d.setDate(base.getDate() + i);\n  return { label, date: fmt(d), total: 0, items: /** @type {any[]} */([]) };\n});\n\n// Group + pre-number\nfor (const t of tasks) {\n  const bucket = days.find(x => x.date === t.date);\n  if (!bucket) continue;\n  const n = bucket.items.length + 1;\n  bucket.items.push({\n    n,                    // numbering to print\n    name: t.name,         // <-- keep name\n    priority: t.priority,\n    desc: t.desc\n  });\n  bucket.total++;\n}\n\nreturn [{ json: { weekTotal: tasks.length, days } }];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -7760,
        8224
      ],
      "id": "ed5a3ac4-dfff-47f0-be59-1817eb14d6ce",
      "name": "Calculate Total Events + Normalize Data"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const strip = s => (s ?? '').replace(/<[^>]*>/g, ' ').replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n\nconst d = $json.data || {};\nconst clean = strip(d.description).slice(0, 200);\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    ...$json,\n    data: { ...d, description_clean: clean }\n  }\n}];"
      },
